{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <fstream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <climits>\n#include <iomanip>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long gcd(long long a, long long b) {\n    if (b == 0) return a;\n    return gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\nlong long lcm(long long a, long long b) {\n    return a / gcd(a, b) * b;\n}\n\ndouble fraction_diff(long long num1, long long den1, long long num2, long long den2) {\n    long long common_den = lcm(den1, den2);\n    long long n1 = common_den / den1 * num1;\n    long long n2 = common_den / den2 * num2;\n    return abs(n1 - n2) / double(common_den);\n}\n\nint main() {\n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    ifstream in(\"input.txt\");\n    ofstream out(\"output.txt\");\n    cin.rdbuf(in.rdbuf());\n    cout.rdbuf(out.rdbuf());\n#endif\n\n    long long x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    long long best_num = 0, best_den = 1;\n    double target = static_cast<double>(x) / y;\n    \n    for (long long d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n        long long lo = 1, hi = 1000000;\n        while (hi - lo > 1) {\n            long long mid = (lo + hi) >> 1;\n            double mid_val = static_cast<double>(mid) / d;\n            if (mid_val < target) lo = mid;\n            else hi = mid;\n        }\n        \n        long long cand = (fraction_diff(lo, d, x, y) > fraction_diff(hi, d, x, y)) ? hi : lo;\n        if (fraction_diff(cand, d, x, y) < fraction_diff(best_num, best_den, x, y)) {\n            best_num = cand;\n            best_den = d;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << best_num << \"/\" << best_den;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\nimport sys\n\ndef gcd(a, b):\n    if b == 0:\n        return a\n    return gcd(b, a % b)\n\ndef lcm(a, b):\n    return a // gcd(a, b) * b\n\ndef fraction_diff(num1, den1, num2, den2):\n    common_den = lcm(den1, den2)\n    n1 = common_den // den1 * num1\n    n2 = common_den // den2 * num2\n    return abs(n1 - n2) / common_den\n\ndef main():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    x = int(data[0])\n    y = int(data[1])\n    n = int(data[2])\n    \n    best_num = 0\n    best_den = 1\n    target = x / y\n    \n    for d in range(1, n + 1):\n        lo = 1\n        hi = 1000000\n        while hi - lo > 1:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            mid_val = mid / d\n            if mid_val < target:\n                lo = mid\n            else:\n                hi = mid\n        \n        cand = hi if fraction_diff(lo, d, x, y) > fraction_diff(hi, d, x, y) else lo\n        if fraction_diff(cand, d, x, y) < fraction_diff(best_num, best_den, x, y):\n            best_num = cand\n            best_den = d\n    \n    print(f\"{best_num}/{best_den}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.007967749610543e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.004126011859625578, -0.03830153867602348, -0.25194117426872253, -0.201773